From: magpie <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov5640: power down for system sleep

The driver only has runtime PM ops (with a 1 s autosuspend). A system
sleep that cuts the core power (the sam9x5 backup sleep) also resets the
PIOs that hold the sensor in power-down and reset, so the sensor can lose
its registers while runtime PM still counts it as powered and configured.
After such a resume the sensor sends no frames, the ISI reset or disable
times out, and the ISI is left enabled with an armed DMA channel. Use
pm_runtime_force_suspend/resume as system sleep ops so the sensor is
powered down before the sleep and set up from scratch on its next use.

Signed-off-by: magpie <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -4008,6 +4008,15 @@
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops ov5640_pm_ops = {
+	/*
+	 * A system sleep can cut the power of the SoC (sam9x5 backup mode) and
+	 * with it the GPIOs that hold the sensor in power-down/reset, so the
+	 * sensor can lose its registers while runtime PM still counts it as
+	 * powered and configured (the 1 s autosuspend often has not run yet).
+	 * Power it down properly before the sleep; the next use powers it up
+	 * and restores the mode from scratch.
+	 */
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(ov5640_sensor_suspend, ov5640_sensor_resume, NULL)
 };
 
